   "content": "<p>//character stream (read) program\n#include &lt;conio.h&gt;\n#include &lt;iostream.h&gt;\n#include &lt;fstream.h&gt;\nint main()\n{\nchar ch;\nifstream reads(&quot;c:\\\\charactersfile.txt&quot;);\nwhile(!reads.eof())\n{\nread.get(ch);\ncout&lt;&lt;ch&lt;&lt;endl;\n}\nread.close();\ngetch();\nreturn 0;\n}</p><p>Output of the program</p><p>r\ne\na\nd\n\nt\nh\ne\n\nf\ni\nl\ne\n\np\nl\ne\na\ns\ne\n.</p><p>ii. Writing files character by character</p><p>Similarly, using single character stream, data can be written to files character by character by using the function put (). Consider the following program that writes data character by character to an empty file “characterswrite.txt”.</p><p>//character stream ( write) program\n#include &lt;conio.h&gt;\n#include &lt;iostream.h&gt;\n#include &lt;fstream.h&gt;\nint main()\n{\nchar ch;\nofstream writes(&quot;d:\\\\characterswrite.txt&quot;);\nfor (int i=0; i&lt;=20; ++i)\n{\ncin&gt;&gt;ch;\ncout&lt;&lt;writes.put(ch);\n}\nwrites.close();\ngetch();\nreturn 0;\n}</p>",
